{
  "_about": "Custom status text up to 80 characters (D07.6, 12.1.17). Byte-identical in the desktop app, Tin Hat Web and Tin Hat Server. `text` stays 1-40 characters so apps and servers from before 12.1.17 still show it; a longer status keeps its whole text (41-80 characters after trim) in `full` and cuts `text` at a whole character (grapheme) to at most 39 characters, drops trailing graphemes that are only spaces and adds U+2026 (just U+2026 when the first grapheme alone is longer). Trimming = JS \\s plus U+0085 = Rust char::is_whitespace plus U+FEFF, in both apps. shorten: what a status write stores (`full` null = no full key). read: what an app shows for a status (null = no status); `old` = the 12.1.15 apps' rule (text 1-40 after trim). server: the GET /api/presence row's `status` (null = none). The editor_cap_* rows (12.1.17 Stage B, the review's #5): the status editors cap a typed or pasted text at 80 code points by WHOLE graphemes (desktop cap_status_edit / web capStatusEdit, vectors status-edit.json), so what they save is at most 80 code points, ending on a whole grapheme; the server keeps such a `full` (it counts code points, 1-80, the same count) and never cuts it.",
